export anchor BBSANSIStyle:
    number: 348
    screen: TeamChat
    name: BBS ANSI
    idea: A chat that behaves like a dial-up message board, drawn in sixteen colour ANSI with shade block banners, double line boxes, hotkey menus and a message reader that counts MSG 1/5.
    base: dark
    palette:
        black: #000000, the page and the label cut outs on box rims
        navy: #000055, side boxes and style sheet boxes
        blue: #0000aa, the message reader box
        dcyan: #00aaaa, message header bars and the current board
        cyan: #55ffff, box rims and info text
        yellow: #ffff55, titles, hotkey letters and the focus block
        white: #ffffff, message text
        grey: #aaaaaa, body text, off-line and the footer bar
        green: #55ff55, the NEW count, ON-LINE and the Send key
        magenta: #ff55ff, mentions and typing
        brown: #aa5500, the hard drop shadow under the title only
    type:
        One monospace stack, Perfect DOS VGA 437, Px437 IBM VGA8, then
        ui-monospace, DejaVu Sans Mono, Liberation Mono, Menlo, Consolas.
        Base 15px at 1.35. The title is 26px bold, tracked 0.12em, yellow
        with a 3px brown drop. Message headers are 15px bold black on
        dark cyan.
    layout:
        A 1200px screen on black. A banner row of light, medium and dark
        shade blocks in blue and cyan, then BRIGHTWORK CHAT in yellow with
        a cyan caller line, then a row of half blocks, clipped by their row.
        Two columns, 350px and the reader, 20px apart. Every region is a
        navy box with a 4px double cyan rim and a yellow label cut into
        the top edge. Message boards lists hotkeys in brackets, G, D, M, B,
        R, the current board on a cyan band marked HERE, mobile-release
        with 4 NEW in green and billing-war-room with @1 FOR YOU in
        magenta. Direct lines lists people with a full block and ON-LINE,
        a half block and AWAY, a dot and OFF-LINE. The reader box is blue
        with a white rim, titled Reading the channel with 5 messages. Each
        message is a framed box whose cyan header bar reads MSG n/5, FROM
        and the name, and the time on the right. Aiko's message adds a
        line with a triangle and 3 REPLIES, read thread, +1 thumbs up x3
        and oo eyes x1. Priya's image is a blocky pixel preview with FILE
        ATTACHED and the filename. Then a magenta typing line and the
        prompt Enter text with the field and three keys, Attach, Emoji
        and a green Send, each with its hotkey letter highlighted. A grey
        footer bar lists the caller, board and keys. Below 780px the
        columns stack.
    spacing: A character grid. 10px between message frames, 20px between boxes.
    density: Busy and full. Every region boxed and a header bar on every message.
    corners: Square.
    borders: 4px double cyan rims with the label cut into the top edge, 1px cyan message frames.
    shadows: Only a hard 3px brown drop under the title text.
    icons: Block glyphs, full block on-line, half block away, dot off-line, triangles for thread and HERE, always with words.
    focus: A solid yellow block with black text.
    tone: Shouty sysop labels, such as 4 NEW, @1 FOR YOU, FILE ATTACHED and Enter text.
